        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "In addition to declaring aspects in your configuration by using either "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<aop:config>"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " or "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<aop:aspectj-autoproxy>"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ", it is also possible to programmatically create proxies that advise target objects. For the full details of Spring’s AOP API, see the "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "next chapter"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "core/aop-api.html"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": ". Here, we want to focus on the ability to automatically create proxies by using @AspectJ aspects."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "You can use the "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "org.springframework.aop.aspectj.annotation.AspectJProxyFactory"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " class to create a proxy for a target object that is advised by one or more @AspectJ aspects. The basic usage for this class is very simple, as the following example shows:"
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "dlist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "// create a factory that can generate a proxy for the given target object\nAspectJProxyFactory factory = new AspectJProxyFactory(targetObject);\n\n// add an aspect, the class must be an @AspectJ aspect\n// you can call this as many times as you need with different aspects\nfactory.addAspect(SecurityManager.class);\n\n// you can also add existing aspect instances, the type of the object supplied\n// must be an @AspectJ aspect\nfactory.addAspect(usageTracker);\n\n// now get the proxy object...\nMyInterfaceType proxy = factory.getProxy();"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "java",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Java"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              },
              {
                "description": {
                  "blocks": [
                    {
                      "context": "listing",
                      "id": null,
                      "inlines": [
                        {
                          "kind": "text",
                          "value": "// create a factory that can generate a proxy for the given target object\nval factory = AspectJProxyFactory(targetObject)\n\n// add an aspect, the class must be an @AspectJ aspect\n// you can call this as many times as you need with different aspects\nfactory.addAspect(SecurityManager::class.java)\n\n// you can also add existing aspect instances, the type of the object supplied\n// must be an @AspectJ aspect\nfactory.addAspect(usageTracker)\n\n// now get the proxy object...\nval proxy = factory.getProxy<Any>()"
                        }
                      ],
                      "language": "kotlin",
                      "roles": [],
                      "title": null
                    }
                  ],
                  "checkbox": null,
                  "inlines": []
                },
                "terms": [
                  [
                    {
                      "kind": "text",
                      "value": "Kotlin"
                    }
                  ]
                ]
              }
            ],
